WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.740
Take 2-bromopropane and
potassium hydroxide.

2
00:00:03.740 --> 00:00:08.520
Warm them in water, and you mainly
get an alcohol: propan-2-ol.

3
00:00:08.520 --> 00:00:12.460
Now dissolve the hydroxide in
ethanol and heat under reflux.

4
00:00:12.460 --> 00:00:16.120
This time, the main
product is a gas: propene.

5
00:00:16.120 --> 00:00:17.260
Same ion.

6
00:00:17.260 --> 00:00:18.800
Same starting compound.

7
00:00:18.800 --> 00:00:21.640
A different solvent,
and a different product.

8
00:00:21.640 --> 00:00:26.280
So why does hydroxide make an alcohol
in water, but a gas in ethanol?

9
00:00:26.280 --> 00:00:30.680
In this mission, you'll see that a
hydroxide ion can do two different jobs,

10
00:00:30.680 --> 00:00:34.040
and how the conditions
decide which one wins.

11
00:00:34.040 --> 00:00:37.960
Then you'll predict every
alkene a bromoalkane can give.

12
00:00:37.960 --> 00:00:42.920
Your mission: explain why ethanol gives
a gas where water gives an alcohol.